From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: port: O/H register + FQ-state readback debugfs verb (phase 1g)

Phase 1g of the O/H-port re-enqueue infra (T-M6-8,
plans/ASK2-VLAN-REARCH.md section 3, Option D). Phase 1f (0183,
board-tested 2026-09-02) produced a clean NULL result: capture_init +
bringup 4 <sink> + enable 4 1 + sched_fq 4 + inject 4 all returned 0
(qman_enqueue() accepted the frame into the O/H port's input FQ), but
the capture sink never saw it arrive -- "capture_fini: ... saw 0
frame(s)". No wedge, no crash, board stayed fully healthy throughout.

That result narrows nothing on its own: qman_enqueue() succeeding only
proves QMan accepted the frame into the software-owned input FQ, not
that the O/H port ever dequeued it. This patch adds one read-only
diagnostic verb to distinguish between three different failure
classes before guessing at a fix:

  (a) the O/H port never dequeued the frame at all (an FMBM_OCFG[EN]/
      channel-id/scheduling problem)
  (b) it dequeued the frame but lost it somewhere downstream in its
      own BMI/parser/enqueue pipeline
  (c) the "bringup"/"enable"/"sched_fq" writes didn't actually stick
      the way this tool has been assuming

New verb "dump <hw_port_id>":
- Reads back the O/H port's own BMI config registers (FMBM_OCFG,
  OFDNE, OFNE, OFPNE, OFQID, OEFQID, OCCB) directly via ioread32be --
  confirms what's actually programmed on silicon right now, not just
  what earlier writes believed they set. Rules in/out failure class
  (c).
- qman_query_fq_np() on the phase-1e input FQ (if sched_fq has run):
  reports frm_cnt/state/byte_cnt. The decisive read: after an
  "inject", frm_cnt still 1 means the O/H port never pulled the frame
  off its channel (class a); frm_cnt back to 0 means it WAS dequeued
  and the loss happened after that (class b).
- The same query on the phase-1f capture sink FQ, for symmetry.

Purely additive and read-only (no register writes, no FQ mutation) --
safe to run at any point after "bringup", independent of whether
sched_fq/capture_init have run yet (each half degrades gracefully with
an informative message if its prerequisite verb hasn't been called).

Board-test plan for the next session: repeat the phase 1f sequence
(capture_init; bringup 4 <sink>; enable 4 1; sched_fq 4) then run
"dump 4" BEFORE "inject 4" as a baseline (expect input frm_cnt=0), run
"inject 4", then "dump 4" again immediately after -- the input FQ's
frm_cnt in that second dump is the answer to which failure class this
is.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (new debug-only,
read-only diagnostic verb extending 0177/0180/0182/0183's existing
tool; no register writes, no FQ mutation, gated behind a manual
debugfs write, RX/TX/existing paths untouched)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c | 79 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 79 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 3e7d10f..f2391ca 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -3075,6 +3075,83 @@ static ssize_t fman_port_oh_test_inject(u8 port_id)
 	return 0;
 }

+/*
+ * ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra (dpaa1), phase 1g: register + FQ-state
+ * readback, added after phase 1f's "inject" produced a clean NULL result
+ * (qman_enqueue() succeeded but the capture sink never saw the frame, no
+ * wedge). This does not guess at a fix -- it narrows which of three
+ * failure classes actually happened: (a) the O/H port never dequeued the
+ * frame at all (config/EN/channel problem), (b) it dequeued but the
+ * frame vanished downstream (BMI/parser/enqueue problem), or (c) the
+ * "bringup"/"enable"/"sched_fq" register writes did not stick the way
+ * this tool assumes.
+ *
+ * "dump <hw_port_id>" prints:
+ * - a raw readback of the O/H port's own BMI config registers (OCFG,
+ *   OFDNE, OFNE, OFPNE, OFQID, OEFQID, OCCB) -- confirms what's actually
+ *   programmed, not just what "bringup"/"enable" believed they wrote.
+ * - qman_query_fq_np() on the port's phase-1e input FQ (if sched_fq has
+ *   run): frm_cnt/state. If frm_cnt is still 1 after an "inject", the
+ *   O/H port never pulled the frame off its channel at all -- failure
+ *   class (a). If frm_cnt is 0, the port DID dequeue it and the frame
+ *   was lost somewhere after that -- failure class (b).
+ * - the same query on the phase-1f capture sink FQ (if capture_init has
+ *   run), for symmetry (expected empty/0 either way in the NULL-result
+ *   case already observed).
+ */
+static void fman_port_oh_test_dump_fq_np(const char *label, struct qman_fq *fq)
+{
+	struct qm_mcr_queryfq_np np;
+	int err;
+
+	err = qman_query_fq_np(fq, &np);
+	if (err) {
+		pr_info("fman_port: oh_test dump: %s fqid=0x%x query_fq_np() = %d\n",
+			label, qman_fq_fqid(fq), err);
+		return;
+	}
+	pr_info("fman_port: oh_test dump: %s fqid=0x%x state=0x%x frm_cnt=%u byte_cnt=%u\n",
+		label, qman_fq_fqid(fq), np.state, np.frm_cnt & 0xffffffU, np.byte_cnt);
+}
+
+static ssize_t fman_port_oh_test_dump(u8 port_id)
+{
+	struct fman_port *port;
+	struct fman_port_oh_bmi_regs __iomem *regs;
+
+	if (port_id >= ARRAY_SIZE(fman_port_oh_input_fq))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	port = fman_port_oh_test_lookup(port_id, true);
+	if (!port) {
+		pr_err("fman_port: oh_test dump 0x%02x: not configured yet (run bringup first)\n",
+		       port_id);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
+	regs = &port->bmi_regs->oh;
+	pr_info("fman_port: oh_test dump 0x%02x: OCFG=0x%08x OFDNE=0x%08x OFNE=0x%08x OFPNE=0x%08x OFQID=0x%08x OEFQID=0x%08x OCCB=0x%08x\n",
+		port_id,
+		ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_ocfg), ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_ofdne),
+		ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_ofne), ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_ofpne),
+		ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_ofqid), ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_oefqid),
+		ioread32be(&regs->fmbm_occb));
+
+	if (fman_port_oh_input_fq[port_id].ready)
+		fman_port_oh_test_dump_fq_np("input", &fman_port_oh_input_fq[port_id].fq);
+	else
+		pr_info("fman_port: oh_test dump 0x%02x: input FQ not scheduled (run sched_fq)\n",
+			port_id);
+
+	if (fman_port_oh_capture.ready)
+		fman_port_oh_test_dump_fq_np("capture", &fman_port_oh_capture.fq);
+	else
+		pr_info("fman_port: oh_test dump 0x%02x: capture sink not created (run capture_init)\n",
+			port_id);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static ssize_t fman_port_oh_test_write(struct file *file,
 				       const char __user *buf,
 				       size_t count, loff_t *ppos)
@@ -3105,6 +3182,8 @@ static ssize_t fman_port_oh_test_write(struct file *file,
 		err = fman_port_oh_test_capture_fini();
 	else if (sscanf(kbuf, "inject %hhu", &port_id) == 1)
 		err = fman_port_oh_test_inject(port_id);
+	else if (sscanf(kbuf, "dump %hhu", &port_id) == 1)
+		err = fman_port_oh_test_dump(port_id);
 	else
 		return -EINVAL;

